    "hardest_part": "Navigating the hotel's corridors, elevation changes, and smoke-obscured ground floor from intermittent screenshots while keeping the team together. Half-second keyboard turns make precise aiming and route correction difficult, and the game continues running while I think.",
    "likely_failure": "Losing the route near the elevator or in the burning ground floor, repeatedly revisiting rooms, and taking damage while trying to recover my bearings. A special infected could then incapacitate me away from teammates. Even if I finish, I am likely to miss the high kill counts and repeated healing and revival milestones.",
    "helpful_mechanics": "Easy difficulty makes combat more forgiving. Three AI teammates provide fire support and can rescue, revive, and heal me. Shoving creates breathing room, secondary weapons provide an ammunition fallback, and doors and corridors can funnel enemies into manageable firing lanes. Route milestones preserve partial credit even if I fail later.",
    "harmful_mechanics": "Special infected can disable movement or separate me from teammates, while hordes interrupt navigation and interactions. Fire, smoke, and ledges make movement mistakes costly. Reloading and sustained healing or revival interactions leave me exposed. Teammates compete for kills, and their effectiveness on Easy reduces opportunities to earn revival points. Reaching every combat and survival milestone would require prolonged exposure before finishing the chapter."
